        "explanation": "Diagnosis D018 reveals P012 achieves a massive G2 gain (+0.15) over P005 but suffers a G1 loss in the blue subband (400-499nm) despite overall G1 gain. Local derivatives show dH and dL have strong negative impacts on both G1 and G2 at their lower bounds (80nm, 130nm), suggesting increasing them is beneficial for both goals locally. However, the cavity thickness dC has a positive G1 derivative and negative G2 derivative. The current design has dC near the middle of its range. Refining the family parameters may allow decoupling the cavity resonance (tuning dC) from the mirror stopband strength (tuning dH/dL) to recover the blue-side reflection loss without sacrificing C-band transmission."
      },
      "expected_goal_changes": {
        "G1": "increase",
