        "diagnosis_id": "diagnosis:eda8bf9d3ca0576912f8b9547916b1bdd41cdb41d0ec8e0c1cf129bb459ef446",
        "observation_ids": ["goal:G1", "goal:G2"],
        "explanation": "P020 (chirped stack F006) shows a G1 loss (-0.008) but a G2 gain (+0.042) compared to P003. The chirp mechanism aims to broaden the stopband. The loss in G1 suggests the passband ripple or edge steepness is suboptimal. By untying the shared variables (dH_start, dH_mid, etc.) into independent layer thicknesses, we can specifically adjust the layer thicknesses responsible for the C-band passband shape (likely the central layers) without disturbing the chirped profile that provides the wide visible rejection. This action tests if the specific chirp profile in F006 is too rigid to simultaneously optimize the narrow C-band pass."
      },
      "expected_goal_changes": {
        "G1": "increase",
        "G2": "unchanged"
      }
    }
  ]
}

